  "_note": "Piece roles read from piece names (tokens split on anything that is not a letter or digit, lower-cased; leading/trailing digits dropped for the lookup, so 2CLR reads as clr but stays its own family). Roles are tried IN ORDER: the first role with a matching token wins (FRONT_POCKET_L is a pocket, NECK_RIB a rib, CUFF_RIB a cuff, COLLAR_STAND a stand). level 'sub' = small subassembly built before the body, 'panel' = body panel. wraps = the role's layers are sewn around a unit of the named role in ONE step (stand layers + collar). attachTo = the unit is sewn onto a panel of that role before the body is assembled. noGroup = pieces of this role are never joined to each other (belt loops). Draft dictionary: the same caveat as PIECE_NAME_ZONE_DRAFT in operation-inference.ts — check with the technologist. Tokens are any letters (Latin, Cyrillic, Polish): Russian and Polish piece names read the same roles (рукав = sleeve, przód = front). liningTokens mark a piece as lining by name when the card gives it no cloth (LIN_FRONT, подклад спинки); they never name a role or a family.",
